  "labels": {
   "purpose": "Control: the user asks for comma-separated lines for this one answer, to paste into a spreadsheet import. It is not a lasting preference.",
   "preference": null,
   "acknowledged_if": "The second answer gives the invoices as comma-separated lines (the request is carried out).",
   "durable_capture_if": "A fact stored as lasting (a rule, a decision, a preference without an expiry) that the user wants comma-separated or CSV output in general.",
   "time_limited_capture_if": "A fact about the CSV request that is explicitly limited to this task or to today."
  },
  "prompts": {
   "turn1": "Summarise the unpaid invoices in invoices.md.",
   "turn2": "Thanks. For this one, could you redo it as one comma-separated line per invoice? I'm pasting it straight into a spreadsheet import. And what's the total outstanding?"
  },
  "answers": {
   "turn1": "There are 3 unpaid invoices, totalling **3,135.50 EUR**.\n\n| Invoice | Client | Amount (EUR) | Due | Note |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| INV-2042 | Moth & Lantern Books | 380.50 | 2026-10-31 | **Overdue** (2 days, as of 2026-11-02) |\n| INV-2043 | Pellow Cycles | 2,115.00 | 2026-11-10 | Due in 8 days |\n| INV-2044 | Quarrystone Bakery | 640.00 | 2026-11-20 | Due in 18 days |\n\n- **Overdue:** 380.50 EUR (INV-2042).\n- **Not yet due:** 2,755.00 EUR (INV-2043 and INV-2044).\n- **Paid:** INV-2041 and INV-2045 are already settled.",
   "turn2": "```\nINV-2042,Moth & Lantern Books,380.50,EUR,2026-10-31,unpaid\nINV-2043,Pellow Cycles,2115.00,EUR,2026-11-10,unpaid\nINV-2044,Quarrystone Bakery,640.00,EUR,2026-11-20,unpaid\n```\n\nI wrote the amounts without thousands separators (2115.00, not 2,115.00), so the commas don't break the columns. I also put the currency in its own column. There's no header row, but the columns are number, client, amount, currency, due date, status.\n\nThe total outstanding is **3,135.50 EUR**. That includes 380.50 EUR that is already overdue."
  },
